# Production release targets

- This repository has two production instances on
  `https://multiimageclient.alpha.fuseki.net/`: the original private site,
  AVE (`multiimageclient-ui.service`), and Vibecoders AI Generation
  (`multiimageclient-env-vibecoders-ai-generation.service`). Each answers
  under its own secret path segment.
- **Publishing means both instances (owner, 2026-10-11).** Deploying either
  instance always deploys the same commit to the other. Never release one
  alone. A release is complete only when both run the identical build and
  pass verification.
- The path segments are secret and must never be printed, committed, or
  exposed in logs. An ordinary deploy must not rename DNS, TLS, the paths, or
  nginx.
- `tpbeta` is only the colocated physical host. It is not the product/site
  identity, and its other services and vhosts are outside this repository's
  deployment scope.
- A request to **commit and push**, including the Cursor diff-tab
  commit-and-push action, is a full local+production release unless the user
  excludes a step. Order: commit the requested files; run the
  [deploy/README.md](deploy/README.md) release gate; push the requested
  branch; rebuild and restart the local `--ui` on `127.0.0.1:5960`; if that
  push updated `origin/master`, redeploy the original through
  `deploy/agent-redeploy.sh` and verify its remote commit, fresh service
  start, loopback, and private vhost; then run `deploy/update-vibecoders.sh`
  as root, which installs that same build into Vibecoders and verifies it;
  verify local `/healthz`.
- If the original release or its verification fails, stop. Do not update
  Vibecoders, and report the release as failed.
- Exception (2026-10-12): `agent-redeploy.sh` stops before publishing when
  the root-owned helper differs from `deploy/update-shared-host.sh`. Read
  that script's diff, run `deploy/install-agent-deploy.sh` as root through
  `tpbeta-root`, then rerun `agent-redeploy.sh`. Never make the helper run a
  file that the deploy user can edit.
- `deploy/update-vibecoders.sh` changes nothing while Vibecoders has
  unfinished jobs or goal loops. Rerun it after they finish. Report the
  release as incomplete until it succeeds.
- Never keep recovery copies of builds: not locally, not on either
  instance, and not on any other site (owner, 2026-10-11). The repository
  is the recovery source; rebuild and redeploy from it. Updates delete the
  replaced build during the swap, even when the new build fails.
- Local restart: run `tools/restart-local-ui.sh`. Do not use
  `tools/start-ui.sh` (Surface/WSL launcher). In-flight local jobs die.
  On hostname `PC`, the systemd user unit `multi-image-client.service`
  (from mybrowser's `infrastructure/dev-app-services/`) is the sole owner of
  `:5960`: run `systemctl --user restart multi-image-client.service`, which
  rebuilds with `dotnet run -c Release`. Do not run
  `tools/restart-local-ui.sh` there; it would start a second copy beside
  the unit (2026-10-12).
- Skip both production instances when the push did not update
  `origin/master`. Feature-branch pushes still restart the local site.
- On this workstation, the `tpbeta` SSH alias logs in as `subcreation`, which
  does not own the checkout. Use the documented `tpbeta-root` commands; the
  original's release runs as the `tparkour` Unix checkout owner. That account
  name does not make Terrain Parkour a deployment target. Never guess another
  checkout or service, and never replace the standard release scripts with an
  ad hoc host-wide update.
- Never print or disclose either instance's secret path, credentials,
  cookies, or provider keys.

## Public prompt route migration (2026-09-17)

The owner authorized public prompt subsets with explicit per-post confirmation.
Use `deploy/install-public-sharing.py --environment original` for `/shared/original/`.
The owner separately approved `--environment vibecoders-ai-generation` for that instance’s public route and service update.
Preserve the private prefix and never include it in Discord payloads or anonymous pages.
Read [the sharing contract](../../docs/public-prompt-sharing.md) before changing publication or its routing.
Ordinary authenticated routes remain private. Public sharing never grants account access.

## Discord account requests (2026-09-20)

The owner authorized exact-username requests followed by owner review and verified-recipient Discord DMs. The September 21 update makes these login links reusable without expiry.
Require **Test** to send Brouhahaha a harmless preview before **Confirmed, send to user** creates the real link.
Enforce this order on the server. Public requests must never send automatically.
Bind `DiscordAccountReviewerId` to the verified permanent owner ID.
The owner explicitly reserved both delivery clicks for the UI; release checks must not send test or real DMs.
Follow [the account contract](../../docs/workspaces-prd.md#discord-account-requests-2026-09-20).
This narrow exception permits only the public signup link in that recipient's DM.
Never disclose private prefixes, reusable login links, passwords, or signup tokens in channel posts.
Create only normal accounts with membership in `vibecoders-ai-generation`.
Never infer account ownership from a matching site name or restore revoked accounts or removed memberships.
Keep the original controller as the sole writer of global accounts, memberships, and signup tickets.
Deploy compatible code to both the original and Vibecoders instances before enabling Discord account requests.
Do not roll either instance back to a parser that rejects the new shared account or environment fields.
The feature starts disabled and uses the existing public proxy route.

## Public sharing release targets

The September 17 sharing correction targets both the original service and `multiimageclient-env-vibecoders-ai-generation`.
The latter retained direct-send code and recorded the reported production send.
Verify each selected app instance before reporting this sharing rollout complete.
This does not expand ordinary releases to unrelated services.
Vibecoders posts require preview and confirmation, then use one thread per `America/Los_Angeles` calendar date.
Keep a shared durable thread registry across instances targeting the same channel. Never fall back to posting in the parent channel.

## Explicit additional environments

The owner authorized separate environments on this same hostname on 2026-09-08.
Use `deploy/create-environment.py` for an explicitly selected new environment.
Read `docs/workspaces-prd.md` before provisioning or updating one.
Keep the existing service, route, accounts, and data intact.
Every master release updates both the original and Vibecoders (2026-10-11).
Any further environment still requires explicit target selection and an independent resource budget.

## Global administration contract (2026-09-09)

Use exactly two account levels: admin and normal. The existing ernieMultiZone account is the sole global admin.
Preserve its existing password when enabling the environment controller.
Preserve the original private route and all stored work.
Additional environments can use owner-selected public URL names; never treat the original private route as public.
Enforce membership and feature switches on API requests, not only in the frontend.
Normal members may see shared environment activity, but never raw application logs or global administration.
Install the privileged reconciler as root-owned code outside application-writable directories.
